        "notes": "Read every proof step, multivariate-normal definition and density supplier, conditional-independence and product/independence interfaces. Positive principal blocks and Schur quadratic form prove residual block positive definite. Gaussian affine residual independent of Z by factored density; residual conditional covariance is constant. Zero off-diagonal yields product law; converse uses bounded sine/cosine at (1,1), nonzero Gaussian transforms and exp(-K12)=1. Empty S omits Z. AC propagated; no singular Gaussian claim. Lauritzen Proposition 4.2 applies to marginal coordinates {i,j} union S; its full-conditioning formula is not asserted for arbitrary S without this marginalization."
