      "risk_review": {
        "status": "complete",
        "reviewer": "alpha-batch-26",
        "notes": "Checked all five steps and all stated rates. Degree cap q<=p-1, q/n->0 gives valid residual sample ranks. Uniform event over ALL triples prevents adaptive-selection bias; count <=p^(q+3) also when binomial terms vanish. Error t=c/4 yields exponent n*c^2>=C0 n^(1-2d); entropy O(n^(1-b)log n) is smaller because 2d<b. Null Fisher test <=sqrt(n)c/4; nonnull >=3c/4 times multiplier eventually >sqrt(n)c/2. Every nonedge has retained-parent separator of size <=q; identical lexicographic records produce same colliders/Meek closure as oracle. q=0 (edgeless graphs), p=2, constant p and b=1 work; sample singular fallback is probability zero under hypotheses. Unknown c_n is explicitly theoretical."
      }
